# TextEdit, through everything a person does with a window: typing by key
# and as text, menus, the clipboard, a context menu, resizing, key repeat,
# and how long a key takes to show.
launch com.apple.TextEdit
window com.apple.TextEdit 60
shot 01-opened
keys Hello from LosOS!
expect-change 5
shot 02-typed
text  Ünïcödé ✓
expect-change 5
shot 03-unicode
key cmd+a
expect-menus Format 15
menu Format > Font > Bold
# A menu item is picked through Accessibility, which on GitHub's Intel
# Macs takes seconds (reading the menus above took 4.6 s there).
expect-change 15
shot 04-bold
key cmd+c
expect-clipboard Hello from LosOS! Ünïcödé ✓ 5
clipboard pasted from the host
key right
key return
key cmd+v
expect-change 5
shot 05-pasted
click 120 90 right
shot-popup 06-context-menu 10
key escape
resize 720 460
expect-size 720 460 10
shot 07-resized
key return
hold . 2000
expect-rate 10
shot 08-held
latency 20
